  icon: {fileID: 2800000, guid: b369ab1b093427e43b1b4a6a9f7ddaa0, type: 3}
  title: 'Lesson: Making a 3D platformer controller'
  sections:
  - heading: 
    text: This lesson contains:<br>-Input detection<br>-3D Physics<br>-Raycast<br>-Animator<br>-Inheritance
    links: []
    icon: {fileID: 0}
    scene: {fileID: 0}
    checkList: []
  - heading: 'Level 1: The basics'
    text: A very basic and unsexy 3D platformer controller using a rough implementation
      of Unity physics and input detections. A good place to start though!
    links:
    - linkText: Unity's documentation on AddForce
      url: https://docs.unity3d.com/ScriptReference/Rigidbody.AddForce.html
    - linkText: Unity's documentation on MovePosition
      url: https://docs.unity3d.com/ScriptReference/Rigidbody.MovePosition.html
    icon: {fileID: 2800000, guid: e1ea804d3de36924cb6f34e556a97750, type: 3}
    scene: {fileID: 102900000, guid: 1e9a0379f1296d14598eee8a3c77f2e6, type: 3}
    checkList: []
  - heading: 'Level 2: Ground detection and snappier jump'
    text: Applying more forces (still in a very simple way) and using a raycast to
      detect if the player is grounded or not allow us to make a more polished controller.
      I rotate the body of the player in the direction it's moving to make it look
      more polished as well.
    links:
    - linkText: Unity's documentation on raycasts
      url: https://docs.unity3d.com/ScriptReference/Physics.Raycast.html
    - linkText: Game dev beginner's video on it
      url: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=B34iq4O5ZYI
    - linkText: Unity's documentation on LookAt
      url: https://docs.unity3d.com/ScriptReference/Transform.LookAt.html
    icon: {fileID: 2800000, guid: e94d5dbc8e7d6a5498cb1740c850afd5, type: 3}
    scene: {fileID: 102900000, guid: 34e8b25ba029f4f479356f495971587e, type: 3}
    checkList: []
  - heading: 'Level 3: Animations, polishing the controls and coins to pick up'
    text: Using a 3D model and animations with the animator component we're taking
      this controller to the next level! I also added a few coins to pick up. Check
      the scene readme to read on all the features this controller implements.
    links:
    - linkText: Unity's documentation on the Animator
      url: https://docs.unity3d.com/6000.1/Documentation/Manual/class-AnimatorController.html
    - linkText: 'Unity''s documentation on the OnTriggerEnter method '
      url: https://docs.unity3d.com/ScriptReference/Collider.OnTriggerEnter.html
    icon: {fileID: 2800000, guid: 63a2a3b29ffb1754d96e29c6b2913859, type: 3}
    scene: {fileID: 102900000, guid: eb6e63f71316b5343a7142aa0545add2, type: 3}
    checkList: []
  loadedLayout: 0
